dialogue founding
title: The first fire
trigger: Founding
speaker commander $commander
speaker first $party:1
speaker second $party:2
speaker third $party:3
speaker knight knight
speaker barbarian barbarian
speaker cleric cleric

node open commander
  Night, a day's ride past Saltmoss. The stolen tithe wagon stands in a ring of gorse with its white paint already scraped with mud, and the three who ran with the Commander sit around a fire they are afraid to make any bigger.
  -> first_word

node first_word first
  The Captain's riders turned back at the ford. They'll be out again at first light, with more of them. Before then I'd like to know who I just stole a wagon for.
  -> who

node who commander
  The orb at the Commander's belt brightens a little in the dark, as it has since the dead lantern in Saltmoss lit again.
  * The truth, then. I died in the Still, a long time ago, and woke there this morning. -> truth
    do: AddTrust $party:2 6
    do: AddTrust $party:1 2
    do: SetFlag founding:truth
  * I don't know much more than you do. My memory comes back in pieces. -> pieces
    do: AddTrust $party:1 6
    do: AddTrust $party:3 2
    do: SetFlag founding:pieces
  * Someone the Choir wants back. That should be enough for tonight. -> guarded
    do: AddTrust $party:3 5
    do: AddTrust $party:1 -3
    do: SetFlag founding:guarded

node truth second
  Died. In the Still. And walked out. Every child on the moors has a story about that vault, and none of them end with somebody walking out.
  -> watch

node pieces first
  Pieces. Fine. I'll take a straight answer with holes in it over a whole one that's lying.
  -> watch

node guarded third
  Good. What we don't know, the Captain can't squeeze out of us. Keep the rest until we're somewhere with walls.
  -> watch

node watch commander
  Someone has to sit up with the fire while the others sleep.
  * Knight. You put yourself between the riders and the wagon at the ford. The watch is yours. -> watch_knight
    if: PartyHas knight
    do: AddTrust knight 7
    do: SetFlag founding:watch_knight
  * Barbarian. You'll hear them coming before any of us. Take the watch. -> watch_barbarian
    if: PartyHas barbarian
    do: AddTrust barbarian 7
    do: SetFlag founding:watch_barbarian
  * Cleric, you've mended every cut since the ford. Sleep. Someone else can watch tonight. -> watch_cleric
    if: PartyHas cleric
    do: AddTrust cleric 7
    do: SetFlag founding:watch_cleric
  * I'll take the first watch myself. None of you asked for any of this. -> watch_self
    do: AddTrust $party:3 5
    do: AddTrust $party:2 2
    do: SetFlag founding:watch_commander

node watch_knight knight
  Gladly. A wall that sleeps isn't much of a wall. Rest, all of you. Nothing comes over that ridge without going through me first.
  -> plan

node watch_barbarian barbarian
  Good. I'd not have slept anyway, not in a Choir wagon with the Captain's dogs on our scent. If anything moves out there, you'll hear me before you hear it.
  -> plan

node watch_cleric cleric
  Kind of you to notice. Healers get thanked after the fight, hardly ever before it. I'll sleep, but wake me if anyone so much as sneezes.
  -> plan

node watch_self third
  A commander who stands watch. Where I'm from, the ones giving orders sleep warm. I'll sit up with you a while anyway.
  -> plan

node plan second
  At first light we run hard down the moor road. It's fast, and every hour we stay near Saltmoss is an hour the Captain gets closer.
  -> plan_other

node plan_other third
  And every rider the Captain has knows that road. The peat cuts are slow, but no white wagon has ever gone that way. Nobody would think to look.
  -> decide

node decide commander
  Both of them look to the Commander.
  * We take the road, and we take it fast. -> road
    do: AddTrust $party:2 6
    do: AddTrust $party:3 -2
    do: SetFlag founding:plan_road
  * The peat cuts. Slow and unseen beats fast and caught. -> cuts
    do: AddTrust $party:3 6
    do: AddTrust $party:2 -2
    do: SetFlag founding:plan_cuts
  * Neither of you is wrong. The road by night, the cuts by day. -> both
    do: AddTrust $party:2 3
    do: AddTrust $party:3 3
    do: SetFlag founding:plan_both

node road second
  That's the answer I wanted. Get the wheels greased; we're gone before the frost lifts.
  -> close

node cuts third
  Then pack light. The peat swallows anything heavy, and I'd rather it didn't swallow us.
  -> close

node both first
  Riding at night with a stolen wagon. Either that's very clever or we'll find out soon that it isn't.
  -> close

node close first
  Whatever we are now, a crew, a caravan, a band of thieves, we're it. We may as well make a proper camp of it.
  -> camp

node camp commander
  By the time the fire burns low there is a pit dug for it, a lookout on the ridge and a wagon nobody calls stolen any more. It is the first Camp.
